---
import ProjectLayout from '../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro'
---
<ProjectLayout slug="fanctal">
  <div class="p11Content">
    <header class="p11Intro">
      <p class="p11Eyebrow" data-i18n="pd.fanctal.introEyebrow">Interactive companion to a research paper</p>
      <p class="p11Lead" data-i18n="pd.fanctal.introLead">The fanctal is a self-similar circular fractal: divide a disk into six sectors, inscribe a tangent child disk in three alternating sectors, and repeat the construction indefinitely inside each child. Explore the family behind it below, or read the summary and download a Python implementation further down the page.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="p11Layout">
      <div class="p11FigureCard">
        <svg id="fanctal"></svg>
      </div>
      <aside class="p11Panel">
        <h3 class="p11PanelTitle" data-i18n="pd.fanctal.paramsTitle">Parameters</h3>
        <div class="p11inputs">
          <div class="field p11InputGroup">
            <input id="p11i1" required="" type="number" min="1" step="1" value="6" placeholder=" ">
            <label class="field-label">\(\text&#123;\textbf&#123;n&#125;&#125;\)</label>
            <p class="p11Hint" data-i18n="pd.fanctal.hintN">Number of angular sectors</p>
          </div>
          <div class="field p11InputGroup">
            <input id="p11i2" required="" type="number" min="0" step="1" value="3" placeholder=" ">
            <label class="field-label">\(\text&#123;\textbf&#123;a&#125;&#125;\)</label>
            <p class="p11Hint" data-i18n="pd.fanctal.hintA">Sectors selected to recurse</p>
          </div>
          <div class="field p11InputGroup">
            <input id="p11i3" required="" type="number" placeholder=" ">
            <label class="field-label" data-i18n="pd.fanctal.depth">\(\text&#123;\textbf&#123;Depth&#125;&#125;\)</label>
            <p class="p11Hint" data-i18n="pd.fanctal.hintDepth">Explicit depth 1–7 (empty = automatic cutoff)</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="p11buttons">
          <button id="p11b1" class="p11Button" data-i18n="pd.fanctal.aboutBtn">About the fanctal</button>
          <button id="p11b2" class="p11Button" data-i18n="pd.fanctal.downloadSvg">Download SVG</button>
        </div>
        <div id="p11ResArea"></div>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <section class="p11AreaSection">
      <h3 data-i18n="pd.fanctal.areaCalc">Area calculation A(r, n, a)</h3>
      <div id="p11AreaCalc" class="p11AreaCalc"></div>
    </section>

    <section id="p11About" class="p11About">
      <h3 data-i18n="pd.fanctal.aboutTitle">About the fanctal</h3>
      <p data-i18n="pd.fanctal.aboutConstruction">The original fanctal divides a disk of radius \(R\) into \(6\) congruent sectors and inscribes, in \(3\) alternating sectors, a tangent child disk; the construction repeats indefinitely inside each child.</p>

      <div class="p11AboutGrid">
        <div class="p11AboutCard">
          <h4 data-i18n="pd.fanctal.resultAreaLabel">Main result</h4>
          <p data-i18n="pd.fanctal.resultAreaText">The shaded area equals \(\pi R^2/4\) — proved by two independent methods. The perimeter added at each generation is invariant, \(\pi R + 6R\), but the sum over all generations diverges.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p11AboutCard">
          <h4 data-i18n="pd.fanctal.generalizationLabel">Generalization</h4>
          <p data-i18n="pd.fanctal.generalizationText">The construction generalizes to a parametric family \(f(r,n,a)\): \(n\) angular sectors, of which \(a\) (preferably alternated) are selected to recurse, with scale ratio \(k(n) = \dfrac&#123;\sin(\pi/n)&#125;&#123;1+\sin(\pi/n)&#125;\). Its closed-form area is \(A(r,n,a) = \pi r^2 \cdot \dfrac&#123;a\left(\frac&#123;1&#125;&#123;n&#125; - k^2\right)&#125;&#123;1 - ak^2&#125;\), valid for every admissible \((n,a)\); setting \(n=6\), \(a=3\) recovers exactly \(\pi R^2/4\).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p11AboutCard">
          <h4 data-i18n="pd.fanctal.dimensionLabel">Fractal dimension</h4>
          <p data-i18n="pd.fanctal.dimensionText">The family's self-similar attractor has Hausdorff dimension \(\dim_H(K) = \dfrac&#123;\log a&#125;&#123;-\log k&#125;\), which equals exactly \(1\) when \(ak=1\) — the same condition connected to the invariant perimeter of the original fanctal.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="p11Paper">
        <p class="p11PaperMeta" data-i18n="pd.fanctal.paperMeta">Yasser Díaz Arcila, Juan Manuel Díaz Gómez, and Elizabeth Solórzano Tovar.</p>
        <p class="p11PaperStatus" data-i18n="pd.fanctal.paperStatus">Manuscript in preparation, currently in the review and submission process to Eco Matemático (UFPS). The link to the full article will be added here once it is published.</p>
        <div class="p11Citation">
          <span class="p11CitationLabel" data-i18n="pd.fanctal.citationLabel">Suggested citation (APA, manuscript in preparation)</span>
          <p class="p11CitationText" data-i18n="pd.fanctal.citationText">Díaz Arcila, Y., Díaz Gómez, J. M., &amp; Solórzano Tovar, E. (in preparation). <em>The Fanctal: Area, Perimeter, and a Generalized Family of Self-Similar Circular Fractals</em>. Manuscript in preparation for submission to Eco Matemático.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="p11License" data-i18n="pd.fanctal.licenseNote">It will be published under a CC BY 4.0 license.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="p11CodeSection">
      <h3 data-i18n="pd.fanctal.codeTitle">Reproduce it in Python</h3>
      <p data-i18n="pd.fanctal.codeIntro">This script implements the same recursive construction described above — sector selection, scale ratio, and termination criteria — so you can regenerate every figure independently, in your own language if you prefer.</p>
      <div class="p11CodeCard">
        <div class="p11CodeToolbar">
          <span class="p11CodeFilename">fanctal.py</span>
          <div class="p11CodeActions">
            <button id="p11CodeToggle" class="p11CodeBtn" data-i18n="pd.fanctal.codeShow">Show code</button>
            <button id="p11CodeCopy" class="p11CodeBtn" data-i18n="pd.fanctal.codeCopy">Copy</button>
            <a id="p11CodeDownload" class="p11CodeBtn is-solid" href="/scripts/fanctal.py" download data-i18n="pd.fanctal.codeDownload">Download .py</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <pre id="p11CodePre" class="p11CodePre" hidden><code id="p11CodeBlock" class="language-python"></code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="p11Related">
      <h3 data-i18n="pd.fanctal.relatedTitle">See also</h3>
      <a class="p11RelatedLink" href="/projects/cantor-sets" data-i18n="pd.fanctal.relatedCantor">Cantor Sets — another fractal in this portfolio</a>
    </section>
  </div>
  <div class="space-bottom"></div>
</ProjectLayout>
<style>@import '../../styles/sections/projects.css';</style>
<style is:global>@import '../../styles/sections/projects-fanctal.css';</style>
<script type="module" is:inline>
  import Fanctal from '/js/lib/Fanctal.js'
  import hljs from 'https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/highlight.js/11.9.0/es/highlight.min.js'

  const p = new Fanctal(); p.starter?.(); p.main()

  const codeToggle = document.getElementById('p11CodeToggle')
  const codeCopy = document.getElementById('p11CodeCopy')
  const codePre = document.getElementById('p11CodePre')
  const codeBlock = document.getElementById('p11CodeBlock')
  let codeText = ''
  let codeLoaded = false

  async function loadCode() {
    if (codeLoaded) return
    codeLoaded = true
    const res = await fetch('/scripts/fanctal.py')
    codeText = await res.text()
    codeBlock.textContent = codeText
    hljs.highlightElement(codeBlock)
  }

  codeToggle?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    await loadCode()
    const willShow = codePre.hidden
    codePre.hidden = !willShow
    const key = willShow ? 'pd.fanctal.codeHide' : 'pd.fanctal.codeShow'
    const fallback = willShow ? 'Hide code' : 'Show code'
    codeToggle.dataset.i18n = key
    codeToggle.textContent = window.i18nGet ? window.i18nGet(key, fallback) : fallback
  })

  codeCopy?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    await loadCode()
    navigator.clipboard.writeText(codeText)
    const original = codeCopy.textContent
    codeCopy.textContent = window.i18nGet ? window.i18nGet('pd.fanctal.codeCopied', 'Copied!') : 'Copied!'
    setTimeout(() => { codeCopy.textContent = original }, 1500)
  })
</script>
